    "instruction": "Continue the SLUGFESTER reassessment campaign with Batch 17 in `/Users/philstilwell/Documents/SLUGFESTER.com`.\n\nBatch 16 completed at commit `08f3e18f4841c4191b12a7f85b1f3a284fa71177`. Begin by confirming that the workspace is clean and local `HEAD`, local `main`, and `origin/main` match.\n\nUse the `reassess-slugfester-debates` skill, the repository’s current frozen workflow and controls, and Batch 16 as the latest precedent. Deterministically select and freeze the next ten eligible, previously unpublished dyadic debates. Do not select Batch 18.\n\nThis prompt is standing authorization for the complete Batch 17 workflow: source preparation and bounded recovery; score-blind inventory; two fresh isolated 5.6 Sol/low judgments per debate; disagreement extraction; required audio verification; adjudication; final-ledger assembly; exactly one deterministic score pass; publication reconstruction and bounded field-level recovery; compilation; rendering verification; compatibility staging; production publication; generated SEO and dependent-artifact correction; complete repository validation; commits; and pushes to `origin/main`.\n\nAll routine confirmations and successful gates are pre-approved. Continue automatically without requesting separate approval for read-only checks, source/hash verification, manifest preparation, activation, isolated subscription-backed model execution, local servers or browsers, deterministic transformations, authorized production writes, derived-file correction, validation, commits, pushes, or cleanup.\n\nAll local and ChatGPT-subscription work is authorized at $0 direct incremental cost. Conditional sequential `gpt-4o-transcribe-diarize` verification is authorized up to $1.00 total for Batch 17. Before the first paid call, report the frozen primary and worst-case cumulative estimates, then continue automatically if both remain within the cap.\n\nAudio-recovery authorization:\n\n- Give each required frozen clip one primary paid attempt.\n- Do not repeat successful calls.\n- If a call fails solely because of a documented transport or service interruption, allow one replacement attempt for that clip.\n- If a long clip again fails at the transport level, allow one final recovery level that divides the exact frozen clip into the minimum number of contiguous, coverage-complete subclips, with at most two subclips and one paid attempt per subclip.\n- Use no other paid retries.\n- For unresolved speaker attribution after successful transcription, use one fresh isolated 5.6 Sol/low shard restricted to that field and its frozen audio evidence. If invalid, one second fresh field-disjoint one-shot shard is authorized.\n- Preserve every failure and all usage evidence.\n\nBounded diagnosed recovery is authorized throughout. Preserve failures, avoid blind repetition, and use the minimum fresh field-disjoint shards. Allow one attempt per shard and at most two ordinary recovery levels. An exceptional third level is authorized only when a failed multi-field shard atomically discards otherwise potentially valid companion fields; recover only the still-unavailable fields with the minimum fresh field-disjoint shards, one attempt each, no retries, and no fourth level.\n\nExact deterministic correction of stale SEO, summaries, sitemaps, calibration analyses, tests, control labels, compatibility classifications, or similar dependent artifacts is authorized. Preserve the original failed or stale artifact when the workflow requires it.\n\nNever rerun the score pass, manually change calculated scores, reuse rejected prose, alter accepted fields, weaken source or validation controls, or select Batch 18. A new score-stability policy failure or opposite-side reversal is a substantive blocker unless an existing debate-specific exception already covers it; preserve the result and stop for new authority.\n\nA controller or server startup failure before any rendering viewport is attempted may be diagnosed and corrected without consuming a viewport attempt, provided the failure is preserved. Freeze, commit, and correctly inventory all 40 rendering screenshots before compatibility execution. Close the browser and server and remove or safely relocate temporary controller files before compatibility classifies repository writes.\n\nFetch before every push, never force-push, and verify local `HEAD`, local `main`, and `origin/main` equality after every push. Do not discard unrelated user changes or reconcile unsafe history automatically.\n\nStop only if:\n\n- the $1.00 paid-service cap would be exceeded;\n- required source identity, transcript completeness, speaker identity, or evidence cannot be established;\n- an allowed model, audio, adjudication, or recovery gate remains invalid after its authorized attempts;\n- a new score-stability exception is required;\n- repository history has diverged and cannot be reconciled safely;\n- or another genuinely substantive blocker requires new authority.\n\nOn completion, report the selected debates and final scores; model and recovery usage; audio results; estimated paid and direct costs; score-pass integrity; publication repairs; rendering and compatibility results; production and generated-file changes; complete repository-validation results; final commit; local/remote equality; and cleanup status. Stop before selecting Batch 18.\n\nFinal-short-batch amendment:\n\nComplete Batch 17 as the final short batch of the four remaining frozen-pool debates, under all existing standing approvals, and stop before Batch 18.",
